WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.160
Let's show the many different ways we

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.800
can work with images in HAX.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.120
First, let's edit the page.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.080
If I know I'm going to need an image

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.120
here at a later point in time, I could

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.640
search for the types of blocks

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:23.080
associated with images.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.480
Basic image, enhanced image, a GIF,

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.200
memes, image galleries, timelines, image

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.440
comparisons, image block quotes, cards,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.680
self checks. There's a lot of different

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.160
options.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.720
So, either I can pick one of those that

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.520
I want to put in the page.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.200
Or, if I already have media with me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.760
in this case

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.200
I could just drag and drop it in. As I

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.920
approach notice that the top search bar

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.560
highlights, but also these areas of the

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.280
page if I was to drop there.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.400
So, I could upload the media here in the

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.480
side and it'll just insert it at the

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.080
bottom of the page.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.720
I could take that image and drop it the

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.520
exact place that I wanted it, which was

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.720
at the top of the page.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.360
And after doing so in either case

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.120
we'll see that it shows up as an

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.760
enhanced image in the sidebar.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.240
So, from there I can modify the source,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:30.600
change the alt text.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.080
After the big win.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.440
Link it to other places, make it look

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.080
like a nice little card outline, and

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.720
offer a caption and citation. So, as we

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.000
add these

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.960
we'll see that the caption

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:52.800
June

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.760
2010.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.720
fills in automatically.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.800
To build a gallery, I could take this

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.640
image and drop it onto an existing one,

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.080
and we see that we get them combined

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.560
into one.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.560
I could also take that original image

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.840
and drop it in the top bar to get a

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.280
series of options as to what I want to

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.240
do with the image.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.480
Which could either be inserting it in

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.920
the page, linking to the underlying

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.000
file, setting it as the media for this

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.200
page,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:31.560
or just upload again.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.160
After uploading any file, I can always

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.520
go under site settings and files to find

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.880
these files after the fact.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.959
So, in the case of that last one, if I

00:02:41.959 --> 00:02:44.040
would have just uploaded that and then

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.959
wanted to put it in the page after the

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:48.360
fact or copy the link, I could just do

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.040
some media management prior to actually

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.040
adding it to the page.
